## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- ##
## Copy this file to .env. The scripts do it for you and say so when they do.
##
## .env is ignored by git. This template is the committed copy, so change both
## when a setting is added.
##
## Every value here is read at build time and baked into the bundle. Changing one
## needs a rebuild, not a restart, which is why the dev server reads it too.
##
## Nothing secret belongs in this file. The bundle is served to anybody who opens
## the page, so treat every value below as published. The session token is a
## cookie the page cannot read, and that is the reason there is no token here.
## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- ##

## Where the client sends every api call.
##
## This has to be an origin the api lists in ALLOWED_ORIGINS, and it has to be
## spelled the same way. A browser treats 127.0.0.1 and localhost as different
## origins, so the two are not interchangeable here.
API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:9000

## Where the dev server binds, and the port it holds.
##
## The host is spelled out rather than left to resolve "localhost", which can
## land on the IPv6 address alone and leave a server that says it is running
## while 127.0.0.1 refuses. Set FRONTEND_HOST to 0.0.0.0 to reach it from another
## machine.
FRONTEND_HOST=127.0.0.1
FRONTEND_PORT=9001

## BUILD_VERSION and BUILD_COMMIT are deliberately not here.
##
## What this file states wins over the environment, so stating either one here
## would pin every build to whatever was written down, and the footer would name
## a commit that is not the one on screen.
##
## Unset, they are not empty: the build takes the version package.json declares
## and the commit git recorded. A release names itself by setting them, and a
## local build says which code it is without being asked.
